{
  "id": "ligny",
  "title": "Ligny",
  "date": "16 June 1815, evening",
  "blurb": "Napoleon himself faces Blücher's Prussians, drawn up on the gentle slope behind the Ligny brook. The marshy, willow-lined Ligne winds from Wagnelée through St-Amand and Ligny toward Tongrinelle, and every village on it is a fortress of stone farms and orchards. Above them the Bussy windmill watches the whole field. Break the centre at Ligny and the Prussian army is finished as a fighting force.",
  "hint": "The brook can be waded anywhere, but slowly; the village bridges are faster. Batter the villages from the Fleurus heights, then send the Guard over at Ligny and climb to the Bussy mill. Watch your right: Thielmann holds Sombreffe.",
